# --- BEGIN user-managed ---
# Project-specific paths Bazel must not descend into — preserved across
# re-bootstrap. Unlike .gitignore, .bazelignore matches literal directory
# paths (no globs), so list each one explicitly. Typical entries are runtime
# data dirs a container creates with host-unreadable permissions, which would
# otherwise fail package traversal with "Permission denied", e.g.:
#   services/postgres/data
# --- END user-managed ---
